                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "221075c4-57e6-3baa-b1e5-97545c14a792",
                        "entry_id": "5efcb8ec-0bab-3527-87f2-e412bfb38e91",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A dinosaur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "494f23e9-5ec6-4838-a109-bfc391f69a14",
                                "sense_id": "221075c4-57e6-3baa-b1e5-97545c14a792",
                                "text": "—genetically uplifted the ancestors of the saurs, and culturally—at least—uplifted the kraken. We are used to thinking of these species as wise and ancient, which indeed they are, but the octopods are their 'Elder Race.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fd9e2f2-f7dd-47b3-9952-b62cfd01aa92",
                                "sense_id": "221075c4-57e6-3baa-b1e5-97545c14a792",
                                "text": "The city-folk had learned not to run screaming at the sight of a 'saur with a human being on it, but they were still in sufficient awe that trouble was unlikely."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dcb797f5-25c9-4a7d-aef8-f9e1b3bdc302",
                                "sense_id": "221075c4-57e6-3baa-b1e5-97545c14a792",
                                "text": "Are there other good candidates for a collective term? Mesosaur might work. Dinosaurs, pterosaurs and other saurs all lived during the Mesozoic Era – the age of reptiles – 252 to 66 million years ago."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18f18a98-0c6a-47ac-9a18-6b50baeac26d",
                                "sense_id": "221075c4-57e6-3baa-b1e5-97545c14a792",
                                "text": "The bird comes cartwheeling out of the forest in a flurry of feathers and leathery wings. Only as it lands, crashing into the reeds at the edge of the river, does Willem realize that it is not a bird, but a winged saur."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86f03b39-ed26-471d-9bb0-3f77f2faa824",
                                "sense_id": "221075c4-57e6-3baa-b1e5-97545c14a792",
                                "text": "Who better to prank with dinosaurs than the king of 'saurs himself?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd0ed10c-6aaa-4a65-8424-1d963cdb3f72",
                                "sense_id": "221075c4-57e6-3baa-b1e5-97545c14a792",
                                "text": "And her most recent tune, \"Dinosaurs in Love,\" is about a pair of smitten 'saurs who find themselves dining at a party just before the apocalyptic event that wiped-out their race."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
